<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title><%= site.name %></title>
    <meta name="description" content="<%= site.summary %>">
    <link rel="canonical" href="<%= site.url %>/">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="name" href="/"><%= site.name %></a>
      <span class="version">v<%= version %></span>
      <a href="<%= site.repo %>">GitHub</a>
    </header>

    <main class="landing">
      <h1><%= site.name %></h1>
      <p class="summary"><%= site.summary %></p>

      <ul class="promises">
        <li>Guides are plain markdown that reads the same on GitHub.</li>
        <li>The manifest is the only list of what exists.</li>
        <li>If the check passes, the site is correct.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>bearings has no theme. Your repo writes the layout; bearings builds the pages, a markdown copy of each, <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> and a search index, and checks every link, anchor, example, constant, image and diagram in them. This site is built by bearings from its own repo.</p>

      <%- featured = pages.find(&:featured) || pages.first -%>
      <p><a class="start" href="<%= featured.url %>"><%= featured.title %> →</a></p>

      <%- groups.each do |group| -%>
      <h2><%= group.label %></h2>
      <dl>
        <%- group.pages.each do |page| -%>
        <dt><a href="<%= page.url %>"><%= page.title %></a></dt>
        <dd><%= page.description %></dd>
        <%- end -%>
      </dl>
      <%- end -%>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
